  "rounding_note": "Band values are Eni's integers in kb/d; in 2015, 2019, 2020 and 2022 the ten bands plus unassigned sum to Eni's stated world total within 1-2 kb/d (their own rounding). 2010, 2021, 2023, 2024 sum exactly.",
  "annotation": {
    "id": "gulf_shutin_annotation",
    "kind": "text annotation above the 2024 column, outside all bands",
    "label": "over 10 mb/d of Gulf output shut in (Aug 2026)",
    "label_lines": [
      "over 10 mb/d of Gulf output shut in",
      "(Aug 2026, IEA), all grades"
    ],
    "volume_mb_d": 10,
    "status": "agency-estimate",
    "source": "IEA Oil Market Report, September 2026 edition (published 11 Sep 2026), Highlights: 'more than 10 mb/d of Gulf output remained shut in amid heightened security risks', referring to August 2026. The August 2026 edition (published 12 Aug 2026) reported 8.3 mb/d still shut in, referring to July 2026. The >10 figure is also used in the Supply section of this dashboard, which cites the IEA latest report.",
    "note": "A text annotation above the 2024 column (outside all bands), not a data series; it does not modify any plotted value. The reported loss spans all grades the Gulf was producing, so the annotation is placed on the whole column, not one band.",
    "simplification": "The shut-in spans several quality classes: Murban is light & medium sour (40.2 API, 0.79% S, per Eni's band definitions); Arab and Basrah heavy are heavy & sour; Arab extra light and the Qatari condensate are lighter grades. First version drew the full volume as a bracket inside the medium & sour band; first fact-check pass (2026-09-24) added disclaimers; second pass moved it to a text annotation outside all bands and removed the unsupported \"most of the loss is medium-sour\" claim from the copy.",
    "allocation": {
      "medium_sour_share_of_shutin": "DROPPED from copy 2026-09-24 (external fact-check, two passes): pass 1 removed 'two-thirds to three-quarters / 25-30%' (no reproducible source; the IEA gives no per-grade shut-in); pass 2 removed 'most of the loss lands there' (listing medium-sour export grades establishes examples, not the volume-weighted composition of lost production). Copy now only names the Gulf's main export grades that sit in the 26-35 API medium band: Arab Light 32.8/1.97 and Arab Medium 30.2/2.59 (Wikipedia, List of crude oil products, accessed 2026-09-24) and Basrah Medium 27.9/3.0 (Petro-Logistics, 'End of an Era: Basrah Light Exports Cease' + EIA Iraq background; Iraq's largest export grade since Jan 2021; Basrah Light export stopped Jan 2022). No proportion of the loss is asserted.",
      "medium_sour_class_share_offline": "DROPPED with the share above (25-30% followed from the unsourced fraction).",
      "provenance_note": "Murban band (light & medium sour) follows from its published specs (about 40 API, 0.7% S) against Eni's band definitions (print p9; light = 35-50 API with sweet <0.5% S, medium sour 0.5-1% S, sour >=1% S); the WER 2025 named-crudes pages (PDF p99, p109) are bubble charts and give no named volumes, so no per-grade shut-in volumes are asserted."
    },
    "date": "2026-09-11",
    "observation_month": "2026-08"
  },
  "band_definitions_note": "Definitions transcribed verbatim from Eni's 'Quality levels - API gravity and sulphur content' table, print p9 (PDF page 11). Page numbers cited throughout are the printed page numbers; the PDF page is the printed page plus 2."
